    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0639" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115G95/6</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1514, Gulf Refining Company informs Department that <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gulflight</hi> was torpedoed without warning while “following British
                    patrol boats to Bishop.” Please ascertain immediately from ship’s officers and
                    crew or other persons whether <hi rendition="#italic">Gulflight</hi> was under
                    convoy or protection of patrol boats, and, if not, what communication passed
                    between them, and why the <hi rendition="#italic">Gulflight</hi> was following
                    patrol boats.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
